    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="1313" n="1299" xml:id="pg1299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1422</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative on the United Nations War
                        Crimes Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15345</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-02">May 2, 1944</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 10.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that at the
                    meeting of Committee II of the War Crimes Commission, held on Friday, April 28,
                    we discussed the possibility of an international court, taking as a basis for
                    the discussion the enclosed plan which was prepared by Mr. Preuss and Dr. de
                    Moor, the representative of the Netherlands. It is very like the one originally
                    prepared in the State Department.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert Pell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d834-a1.xml" xpointer="d834-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
